# /tempora help
tempora.command.help.description=Lists every Tempora command, or shows how to use one, e.g. /tempora help region set. A ? after any command shows the same, e.g. /tempora lookup ?
tempora.command.help.arg0=Optional. The command to explain, e.g. lookup or region set.
tempora.command.help.label.description=Description: %s
tempora.command.help.label.usage=Usage: %s
tempora.command.help.label.example=Example: %s

# /tempora lookup
tempora.command.lookup.description=Shows the latest events around you and draws them in the world. Every filter is optional and they can go in any order. By default it searches 10 blocks around you, over the last 3 days, in every logger, by anyone, and shows the latest 5 events of each. Loggers that aren't tied to a place, such as weather, are shown by /tempora global instead.
tempora.command.lookup.arg0=How many blocks around you to search, default 10.
tempora.command.lookup.arg1=How far back to look, e.g. 30m, 6h, 1d, 2w, default 3d. A range such as 3d-1d looks between 3 days and 1 day ago.
tempora.command.lookup.arg2=Which loggers to search, comma separated, e.g. break,place. Default is every logger.
tempora.command.lookup.arg3=Whose events to show, comma separated, e.g. Player,Kyium. A ! leaves a player out instead, e.g. !Player for everyone but Player. Block changes and explosions go by the closest player. Loggers with no player, such as mob spawns, are skipped. Default is anyone.
tempora.command.lookup.arg4=How many events to show from each logger, up to 50, default 5.
tempora.command.lookup.nothing_found=Nothing was logged within %s blocks of you %s.
tempora.command.lookup.global_logger=%s isn't tied to a place, so it can't be looked up around you. Use %s instead.

# /tempora global
tempora.command.global.description=Shows the latest events from loggers that aren't tied to a place, such as weather and TPS. Works from anywhere, including the server console. Every filter is optional and they can go in any order. By default it shows the last 10 events of each, over the last 3 days.
tempora.command.global.arg0=How far back to look, e.g. 30m, 6h, 1d, 2w, default 3d. A range such as 3d-1d looks between 3 days and 1 day ago.
tempora.command.global.arg1=Which loggers to show, comma separated, e.g. weather,tps. Default is every one.
tempora.command.global.arg2=How many events to show from each logger, up to 100, default 10.
tempora.command.global.nothing_found=Nothing was logged %s.
tempora.command.global.positional_logger=%s records events at a place, use %s to look them up around you.

# /tempora home
tempora.command.home.description=Finds the chunk a player has spent the most time in, from their position history. Useful for finding their base.
tempora.command.home.arg0=Name of the player to look up.
tempora.command.home.arg1=Optional. Only use positions from this far back, e.g. 1mo, 2w.
tempora.command.home.arg2=Optional. Only look in this dimension.
tempora.command.home.result=Player %s is most active in dimension %s, click %s to visit the location.
tempora.command.home.no_db=Player position logging is disabled, so there is no position history to search.
tempora.command.home.no_data=No position data found for that query.

# /tempora sql
tempora.command.sql.description=Runs a read-only SELECT query against a logger's database and shows the results in chat, for investigations /tempora lookup can't express.
tempora.command.sql.arg0=A read-only SELECT query. The table name is the full logger name, e.g. PlayerPositionLogger.
tempora.command.sql.select_only=Only SELECT queries are allowed.
tempora.command.sql.invalid_table=The query must name a logger table: %s.
tempora.command.sql.missing_columns=Query missing required columns: %s
tempora.command.sql.missing_columns.advice=It is highly recommended to use SELECT * instead of specifying columns.
tempora.command.sql.no_results_in=No results found in %s.
tempora.command.sql.error=SQL error: %s
tempora.command.sql.query_quantity=Found %s matching results.
tempora.command.sql.query_quantity_if_max=Showing the first %s results (server limit: %s). Additional matches may be hidden.

# /tempora wand
tempora.command.wand.description=Gives you a Tempora wand. Left click a block to see its history, right click a face to see the history of the space in front of it.
tempora.command.wand.given=You have been given a Tempora wand. Left click a block to see its history, right click a face to see the space in front of it.

